From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 16:39:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] recore: load BL31 into DRAM to make room for Klipper

We build TF-A with SUNXI_BL31_IN_DRAM=1 so BL31 links at 0x40000000, out of
the low memory Klipper wants; u-boot must load it there to match.

Up to v2024.01 that meant patching #define BL31_ADDR into
arch/arm/dts/sunxi-u-boot.dtsi. From v2026.07 the FIT reads the Kconfig
symbol SUNXI_BL31_BASE for load and entry - but that symbol is declared
"hex" with no prompt, so it is not user-settable and a defconfig line for it
is silently ignored. Give it a prompt, then set it.

Getting this wrong is quiet and fatal: the default 0x00044000 loads a
DRAM-linked BL31 into SRAM, BL31 emits repeated "mmap_add_region_check()
failed. error -12", hands off to 0x4a000000 and u-boot never prints a
banner. Verified on 0498.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig | 2 +-
 configs/recore_defconfig    | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
index ceba96b6..8d782b89 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
@@ -258,7 +258,7 @@ config SUNXI_RVBAR_ALTERNATIVE
 	irrelevant there, and we can use the same code.
 
 config SUNXI_BL31_BASE
-	hex
+	hex "BL31 (TF-A) load address"
 	default 0x00044000 if MACH_SUN50I || MACH_SUN50I_H5
 	default 0x40000000 if MACH_SUN50I_H616
 	default 0x00104000 if SUN50I_GEN_H6
diff --git a/configs/recore_defconfig b/configs/recore_defconfig
index d07d1dc1..bd1adce9 100644
--- a/configs/recore_defconfig
+++ b/configs/recore_defconfig
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ CONFIG_ARM=y
 CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_SPL=y
 CONFIG_MACH_SUN50I=y
+CONFIG_SUNXI_BL31_BASE=0x40000000
 CONFIG_MMC=y
 CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA=2
 CONFIG_RESERVE_ALLWINNER_BOOT0_HEADER=y
-- 
2.47.3

